# step record's clears: hold REC and press OCT- to go back and clear that step (a backspace), OCT+ to clear the
# cursor's step and go on (a rest); OCT+ / OCT- alone skip and go back, the steps kept; REC's release after them is
# not a tap, so step record stays on. Notes from MIDI (channel 2: T2), as midisteprec.xy
wait 300
turn ALGO 1
expect trk 2
tap REC
wait 60
midi 91 3C 64
midi 81 3C 00
wait 40
midi 91 40 64
midi 81 40 00
wait 40
midi 91 43 64
midi 81 43 00
wait 40
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect note 2 1 2 64
expect note 2 1 3 67
# REC + OCT-: back to step 3, cleared; the next note lands there
press REC
tap OCT-
release REC
wait 40
expect note 2 1 3 0
midi 91 45 64
midi 81 45 00
wait 40
expect note 2 1 3 69
# OCT- alone, three times: back to step 1, nothing cleared; REC + OCT+ clears step 1 and goes on to step 2
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
wait 40
expect note 2 1 1 60
expect note 2 1 2 64
press REC
tap OCT+
release REC
wait 40
expect note 2 1 1 0
expect note 2 1 2 64
# OCT+ alone skips step 2 (kept); the next note writes step 3, so step record is still on
tap OCT+
wait 20
midi 91 47 64
midi 81 47 00
wait 40
expect note 2 1 2 64
expect note 2 1 3 71
